{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779472751,"nonce":"R3qTvTwB9Dnps3Qez5uuJ57WLy8=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDH9PLw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/157","origin":"github"},"title":"nav stack activation race: local_costmap times out waiting for sea_surface_estimator's first map_tide TF","message":"## Summary\n\nThe nav-stack bringup on BizzyBoat suffers a lifecycle activation race between `local_costmap` and `sea_surface_estimator`: `local_costmap.on_activate` waits for `bizzy/map_tide` TF but the `sea_surface_estimator` typically publishes its first `map_tide` ~5-10 s after node start, missing the costmap's default ~5 s `wait_for_transform` window. Activation fails silently and the entire navigation stack remains inactive until the user manually retries — sometimes multiple times.\n\nOut of #150 topic 6 closure analysis (`~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-21/`). Same root-cause family as #135.\n\n## Evidence (2026-05-21 deployment)\n\nAfter the §12 stack restart at 13:09 EDT, four bringup attempts were needed before the nav stack reached Active:\n\n| Time (EDT) | Attempt | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| 13:11:15 | #1 | `local_costmap` Activating → TF timeout, no bond |\n| 13:32:13 | #2 | fails (no bond) |\n| 13:34:37 | #3 | fails |\n| 13:37:00 | #4 | **succeeds** — all servers bond, stack healthy |\n\nTrackline launch attempts at 13:25:47 / 13:26:12 EDT were rejected during this window (\"Action server is inactive. Rejecting the goal\").\n\nCritical timing: `map_tide` TF first appeared at +6 s after bag-2 start (13:11:20 EDT); `local_costmap` had already given up by then. (Costmap default `wait_for_transform` is ~5 s.)\n\n**Not** a multi-instance `sea_surface_layer` segfault — that hypothesis was refuted by the bag (all four layer instances initialized cleanly with `Matching size of SeaSurfaceLayer to parent costmap` messages, no crash, no error).\n\n## Operator impact\n\nA boat reboot in the field requires up to ~26 min of \"Action server is inactive. Rejecting the goal.\" spam before the stack finally activates. With students present, this looks like a hard failure with no useful error message in the operator UI.\n\n## Fix candidates\n\nIn rough priority order:\n\n1. **Placeholder `map_tide` TF at sea_surface_estimator startup** (cleanest engineering). The estimator broadcasts an immediate zero-tide `map_tide` at `on_activate`, refining as real data arrives. Eliminates the race. Code change in `mru_transform/mru_transform/nodes/sea_surface_estimator.cpp`.\n2. **Lifecycle dependency / topic-readiness check**: gate `local_costmap` activation on `sea_surface_estimator` having published at least one TF. Requires a small wrapper or a topic-presence service check.\n3. **Patient costmap activation**: increase `local_costmap`'s TF-wait tolerance to ~15-30 s. Bizzyboat-config-only change (`bizzyboat.yaml`). Cheapest but masks the race rather than fixing it; risks slower failure surfacing for real TF problems.\n4. **Launch-script delay**: insert a ~10 s sleep between core bringup and nav-stack bringup in `core_launch.py` / launch script. Cheapest field workaround.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nFor the **June 4 class deadline**: ship option 3 or 4 as an immediate field workaround. Option 4 is least invasive; option 3 surfaces the tolerance as a tunable.\n\nFor the **durable fix**: option 1 in `mru_transform`. It's the right place — startup ordering shouldn't be the consumer's problem.\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter fix:\n\n- Boat reboot leads to nav stack reaching Active in ≤ 10 s (vs current ≤ 26 min worst case).\n- `bt_task_navigator` \"Action server is inactive\" rejections stop appearing in `/rosout` immediately after lifecycle bringup.\n- Trackline launches accepted on first try post-boot.\n\n## References\n\n- 2026-05-21 deployment data: `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-21_deployment.db`\n- Topic 6 closure analysis: this issue's parent comment on #150\n- Original root-cause discovery: #135\n- `sea_surface_estimator` source: `mru_transform/mru_transform/nodes/sea_surface_estimator.cpp`\n\nPart of #150 (topic 6).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}